   500	### 5.5 Graph compile and validation
   501	
   502	Compile when registry, enabled capabilities, formats, or viewport
   503	resource shape changes — not once per ordinary frame.
   504	
   505	Validation fails closed on:
   506	
   507	1. duplicate pass/resource/family IDs;
   508	2. cycles or unstable topological ties;
   509	3. read-before-produce, illegal usage flags, incompatible formats, or a
   510	   sampled/storage-read and writable-attachment alias on the same
   511	   subresource;
   512	4. more or fewer than one presentation terminal;
   513	5. a registered drawable without geometry/pick ownership;
   514	6. an overlay without anchor/metric/hit/depth policy;
   515	7. a clocked family without an injected clock and stop condition;
   516	8. a family whose pick order cannot be derived from scene order;
   517	9. undeclared readback or GPU→CPU synchronization in the hand path;
   518	10. an enabled resource with no lifetime/budget owner.
   519	
   520	### 5.6 Executor loop
   521	
   522	The stable loop is deliberately boring:
   523	
   524	1. receive a scheduler pulse with explicit causes and time;
   525	2. snapshot the world/registry/resource revisions once;
   526	3. select the already-compiled plan for enabled capabilities;
   527	4. collect registered batches; cull and stable-sort by plan order;
   528	5. compute invalidated resources/regions from declared causes;
   529	6. encode each due pass in topological order;
   530	7. submit once, present once, and enqueue only declared asynchronous
   531	   readbacks;
   532	8. record plan hash, revision set, causes, clock, batches, resources,
   533	   and environment fingerprint for replay.
   534	
   535	No atom may recursively request a draw while the frame is encoding.
   536	It invalidates data or registers a future deadline at an edge; the
   537	scheduler coalesces the work.
   538	
   539	### 5.7 Scheduler contract
   540	
   541	The scheduler owns **when** a compiled graph executes, not what the
   542	scene means. It supports these cause classes:
   543	
   544	- `:world` — durable/material or camera/world projection changed;
   545	- `:viewport` — size, DPR, color/format, or device state changed;
   546	- `:resource` — font/image/mesh/pipeline upload or compile became ready;
   547	- `:interaction` — pointer preview, hover, selection, drag, or chrome
   548	  changed without a durable world change;
   549	- `:clock` — one or more registered regions/overlays have a due
   550	  animation deadline;
   551	- `:readback` — golden capture, export, thumbnail, eyedropper, or probe;
   552	- `:device-recovery` — resources/plan must be recreated.
   553	
   554	Rules:
   555	
   556	1. Coalesce causes to at most one normal encode per RAF opportunity.
   557	2. Sleep when there is no invalidation, deadline, or readback. Do not
   558	   turn motion into an always-on global loop.
   559	3. A clocked region registers `next-deadline`, target cadence, and stop
   560	   predicate. Region cadence may differ; the compositor samples the
   561	   most recent completed region texture.
   562	4. Hand-regime interaction is highest latency priority; settle/resource
   563	   work may be deferred or budgeted but not starved.
   564	5. No ordinary frame performs synchronous GPU readback.
   565	6. Replay injects recorded logical time and cause order; shader wall
   566	   time never becomes material truth.
   567	7. Deterministic tie-breaking never depends on map iteration, promise
   568	   completion race, or registration call order.
   569	8. A pass is absent only when its capability is explicitly disabled by
   570	   the compiled capability/material set. Once a committed capability is
   571	   enabled for a rung, failure records the resource/pass and halts that
   572	   rung for repair; the executor may not recover by skipping the pass,
   573	   dropping the capability, or shrinking the graph. The campaign
   574	   continues after repair under §0.
