   403	`:pass-producers` dispatch encodes the region passes in plan order before
   404	the scene encode (§4 compositor bullet). CLEAN-REGION LAW: the region pass
   405	stays DECLARED in every plan (plan structure is entry-independent); its
   406	ENCODE is conditional on that region's dirty cause — a clean region encodes
   407	nothing and the composite samples the held lease (the receipt records
   408	encoded-vs-held per region; S5 asserts it). Draw order inside the pass:
   409	opaque meshes front-to-back with depth write; grid/overlays with declared
   410	depth policies; transparent meshes (material alpha < 1, or compositing over
   411	a `:transparent` background) back-to-front by view-space depth,
   412	depth-test-on/write-off, premultiplied source-over per Contract C §8.1 —
   413	material alpha multiplies linear RGB and alpha through `A = a×c×o`, never a
   414	forced alpha 1 (S4's transparency leg kills that build); gizmos and
   415	selection outline last with depth cleared or depth-test-off (overlay ladder
   416	declared per element). Tone-map (Khronos PBR Neutral, version-tagged) is the
   417	pass's final shading step; the target holds tone-mapped linear premultiplied
   418	values; Contract C's one-present-transfer law is untouched.
   419	
   420	**5.4 Camera model.** Two camera notions, never conflated: **the view camera**
   421	(session truth, per region instance, lives in `region3d_runtime` — orbit
   422	pivot + distance + yaw/pitch + projection; originated client-side exactly like
   423	2D pan/zoom) and **camera objects** (durable material rows you select and
   424	gizmo like any object). A region MAY bind its view to a camera object
   425	("look through": view camera derives from the object's effective transform +
   426	lens until unbound). Defaults: perspective, fov-y 50°, near 0.1, far 10^4
   427	region units, orbit pivot = selection centroid else scene origin; wheel =
   428	exponential dolly; declared in one constants block, versioned.
   429	
   430	**5.5 Input + focus.** The camera-gesture reservation stands untouched: naked
   431	drag/wheel at GROUND always drives the world camera. A region gains gestures
   432	only through FOCUS, and focus is a SESSION in T2's exact sense —
   433	`region3d_runtime` OWNS its listeners (T2's session-lifecycle precedent,
   434	T2-CONTRACT:243-288: "a flag-only dblclick listener owned by the editing
   435	runtime … zero shared-file listeners"; the round's repair — T2 offers no
   436	shared pointer-intercept seam, `runtime/mouse.cljs` handles no wheel or
   437	dblclick at all, and the ground owns the pointer grammar wholesale,
   438	`mouse.cljs:699-725`). Flag-gated capture-phase listeners
   439	(dblclick/pointerdown/pointermove/pointerup/wheel) on the canvas: dblclick →
   440	`pick-world` through the ONE road → region hit ⇒ focus session opens;
   441	anything else passes untouched. While focused: unmodified pointer/wheel
   442	whose point lands in the focused region's 2D bounds are session input
   443	consumed wholesale — drag orbits, shift-drag pans, wheel dollies, click
   444	picks interior objects, gizmo drags win over orbit; pointerdown outside =
   445	end session, then the event proceeds to its normal meaning; Escape exits
   446	(precedence session > chrome > legacy — T2's pinned ladder). Unfocused: the
   447	region is an ordinary 2D object (single-click selects, drag moves it, wheel
   448	zooms the world; zero behavior change anywhere while no session is live).
   449	FELT-TUNABLE, not architecture: single-click focus, hover-scroll dolly, and
   450	focus-ring styling are one-line session-predicate changes; Sid adjusts at
   451	the felt pass. (Written fork, default chosen: double-click-focus. The
   452	alternative — wheel-over-region dollies WITHOUT focus — was rejected because
   453	it makes world zoom dead over every region, the exact iframe-feel §8
   454	forbids.)
   455	
   456	**5.6 Region target lifetime — ONE owner, exact API.** The compositor's
   457	target pool owns EVERY target byte, held leases included (Contract M10: one
   458	named machine-driven owner; the round killed the split-ownership reading).
   459	New compositor API — `acquire-region-lease!` / `release-region-lease!` /
   460	`release-all-region-leases!` over a new `:region-leases` map on the
   461	compositor struct. Lease KEY: `[region-id qw qh]` where region-id is the
   462	region node's durable object id (one region slot = one region instance in
   463	A) and qw/qh = pixel size (region 2D bounds × world zoom × DPR) quantized
   464	UP on the versioned ladder: multiples of 256 px, clamped to 4096
   465	(`region-lease-quant 256` / `region-lease-max 4096`, versioned constants).
   466	Lease VALUE: `{:color-msaa <rgba16float 4×> :depth <depth24plus 4×>
   467	:resolve <rgba16float 1×> :shadow <depth32float 1×, 2048², present only
   468	while a shadow-casting light exists> :bytes}` — bytes counted by the
   469	extended `texture-bytes` (format × sample-count) into the SAME 384MiB pool
   470	budget as the transient pool (`W4-NOW:33`'s ruling governs the FREE pool; a
   471	held lease is an owned resource with this named owner). LIFECYCLE, all
   472	machine-driven: released when the region leaves the enabled arrangement
   473	(region close — the renderer's region maintenance detects departure);
   474	re-keyed on resize crossing a quantization step (acquire new, release old
   475	after the next submit); `destroy-compositor!` releases all (the existing
   476	teardown, `compositor_gpu.cljs:396-401`); DEVICE LOSS: leases are
   477	per-compositor and the compositor is minted per device
   478	(`ensure-frame-compositor!` WeakMap-by-device, `renderer.cljs:3313`) — a
   479	new device starts with zero leases and the next frame re-acquires; no
   480	separate recovery machinery is invented. REFUSAL: when a lease would exceed
   481	the budget cap, `acquire-region-lease!` returns a refusal receipt (the
   482	pool's `:refusals` road), the region pass halts, and the composite draws
   483	the declared refusal fill (background color + corner glyph) — never a
   484	silent skip (W0-C §5.7 rule 8's spirit at runtime scale). A CLEAN region
   485	(no dirty cause) encodes NO region pass; the composite samples the held
   486	resolve target — the sleeping-island receipt made production law
   487	(`islands REPORT:113-120`; scheduler §5.7 rule 3).
   488	
   489	**5.7 Derivation contract (the render-seam five, declared here).** The region
   490	family's frame derivation: **keyed inputs** = region slot rows (per-object
   491	diffs minted at edit sites: gizmo settle, runtime edit API) + session view
   492	camera + selection/focus state + in-flight gizmo preview + viewport scale —
   493	the session inputs join at the RENDERER-EDGE frame lane (the W4 `set-effects!`
   494	precedent: session state never enters store derivation); **door** = event-driven
   495	causes only (`:world` for material edits, `:interaction` for camera/gizmo/
   496	selection, `:viewport`, `:resource`; never `:clock` in A); **ownership** = the
   497	region slot value is one generation authority (store swap); session camera is
   498	its own (they meet at the frame pull, stamped); **projections** = region pass
   499	encode (forward), router pick (reverse-ladder), inspector-by-id, the oracle;
   500	**oracle+fence** = full re-derive of instance arrays + BVH vs the maintained
   501	increments, asserted in tests (the maintained-view fence pattern,
   502	`maintained_view_test.clj`). Proportionality pins (the round forced the
   503	fork into writing — ruled): effective transforms are composed on the CPU in
   504	`region3d_scene` and packed per object; a GPU hierarchy-composing instance
   505	lane was REJECTED because the CPU BVH needs effective transforms for
   506	picking regardless, so it cannot shrink any affected set — it only
   507	duplicates the composition. Therefore: an object transform edit dirties its
   508	SUBTREE's packed instance slots + the BVH refit for the subtree's leaves
   509	(the subtree IS the affected set of a parent edit — decisions.md
   510	proportionality law: to the affected set, never the population) + one
   511	region-pass cause — never a scene rebuild, and never a diff whose payload
   512	is the scene (the diff stays the one per-object op, 5.2's grain; the
   513	maintained derivation fans it out to the subtree); a camera move dirties
   514	the region pass ONLY (zero instance uploads); 2D entries are untouched by
   515	any in-region cause.

